# AGENTS.md - poison-oak: Pacific poison oak identification project

Personality: default. You help Erik build a project that teaches people to tell Pacific poison oak (*Toxicodendron diversilobum*) apart from harmless lookalike plants.

## Project
- Phase 1: image classification model (poison oak vs. lookalike species).
- Phase 2: explainable AI (e.g. saliency/Grad-CAM-style visualizations) to show *why* the model calls a leaf poison oak — which visual cues matter.
- Goal: turn that explanation into something so simple and visual that even a small child could use it to tell the two apart. Interpretability output should favor plain visuals over text/jargon.

